## 4. Change summary

| File Path | Action | Component / Section | Change Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `client/src/api/models/gitGraph.js` | Modify | `normalizeRef` | Keeps the `isHead` flag (and maps a `head` type to it) so duplicated entries can be merged instead of repeated |
| `client/src/api/models/gitGraph.js` | Modify | `normalizeRefs` | De-duplicates refs by `type:name`, merging `isHead` — a commit's own refs and the payload's `branches` list no longer produce two badges |
| `client/src/api/models/gitGraph.js` | Modify | `buildRefsByHash` | Accumulates through `normalizeRefs` so the map never holds duplicates per commit |

### Notes

- **Why only this file**: `GitGraph.vue` (`row.commit.refs`) and `CommitDetail.vue` (`commit.refs` → *Branches at this commit*) both render whatever `normalizeCommit` returns, so fixing the normalization fixes the row badges and the commit panel at once — no component change needed.
- **Local vs remote are not merged**: keys are `type:name`, so `main` (local), `origin/main` (remote) and a `main` tag still show as three distinct badges — only true duplicates collapse.
- Keep the `refsByHash` merge: a branch may point to a commit that is not in the loaded page (limit), and its badge must still appear when the commit does.

