## Changes

**New file** `src/components/ConfirmDialog.vue` — daisyUI modal wrapper (promise-free, purely presentational): icon + title header, message, optional file list, optional hint, Cancel/Confirm in the footer, `busy` state, ESC and backdrop close, focus parked on **Cancel** (safe default for destructive actions).

**`GitView.vue`** — `window.confirm` replaced by `confirmAction()`, a promise-based helper backed by `confirmRequest` state; a `<ConfirmDialog>` is rendered from that state. Covers discard, delete branch, merge-into-current and rebase.

**`RepoFileDiff.vue`** — `window.confirm` replaced by a local `confirmRollback` flag + the same dialog.

### Why this shape

| Concern | Decision |
| --- | --- |
| Native dialog | `confirm()`/`alert()` are unstyled, blocking, and inaccessible on some platforms — replaced by the app modal |
| Reuse | One `ConfirmDialog` used by both components (repo file rollback + git view operations) |
| Promise ergonomics | `await this.confirmAction({...})` keeps the existing handler flow (`if (!accepted) return`) instead of callback spaghetti |
| No orphan promises | A new request settles the previous one with `false`; `beforeUnmount` also settles it |
| Safety | Focus starts on **Cancel**, destructive actions use `btn-error`, the reason/hint is spelled out in the dialog instead of the tooltip |

