## Change summary

| File Path | Action | Component / Section | Change Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `src/components/ConfirmDialog.vue` | Create | `ConfirmDialog` | Reusable confirmation dialog on top of the global `<modal>`: icon + title header, message, optional affected-items list (`maxDetails`, "+ n more"), optional consequence hint, Cancel/Confirm footer, `busy` spinner, ESC/backdrop close, initial focus on **Cancel** |
| `src/components/repo/GitView.vue` | Modify | `confirmAction`, `resolveConfirmation`, `confirmRequest` | Promise-based confirmation replacing `window.confirm`; a new request settles the pending one and `beforeUnmount` resolves it as `false` |
| `src/components/repo/GitView.vue` | Modify | `discardPaths` | Modal with the affected paths, `btn-error` "Roll back" and the untracked-files warning |
| `src/components/repo/GitView.vue` | Modify | `deleteBranch` | Modal explaining that unreachable commits are lost |
| `src/components/repo/GitView.vue` | Modify | `onCommitBranchAction` | Merge and rebase confirmations now use the modal (`btn-warning`, rebase warns about rewritten hashes) |
| `src/components/repo/GitView.vue` | Modify | template | `<ConfirmDialog>` rendered from `confirmRequest` state |
| `src/components/repo/RepoFileDiff.vue` | Modify | `rollback`, `runRollback`, `confirmRollback` | `window.confirm` replaced by the dialog; the flag is reset in `reset()` so switching files never leaves it open |

### Notes

- **No native dialogs left in the git UI**: `confirm()`/`alert()` are gone from `GitView.vue` and `RepoFileDiff.vue`. The remaining `alert alert-error` / `alert-success` blocks are DaisyUI inline banners (operation feedback), not confirmations, so they stay.
- **Safe defaults**: the dialog parks focus on **Cancel**, closes on `Esc` and on backdrop click (both handled by the shared `Modal`), and destructive actions use `btn-error`.
- **No orphan promises**: `confirmAction()` settles a previous pending request with `false` before opening a new one, and `beforeUnmount` does the same, so an `await` can never hang.
- Outside the git UI, `src/components/security/AccountSettings.vue` still calls `alert('Passwords do not match')` — out of scope of this change; say the word and I'll migrate it to the same dialog.

